{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion","id":526479,"title":"Night Doctor Surgery discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-24T02:27:39-07:00","id":526479,"title":"Night Doctor Surgery discussion","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526359#post526359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As an aside, given the Ordo's extensive experience with vampire physiology, I never quite understood why they were unable to choose the Night Doctor Surgery Merit (V 2e, pp. 113-14 ). In many ways, this merit appears more appropriate to many Ordo vampires than to the Carthians.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526361#post526361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would be happy to explain why I feel it's more appropriate as a Carthian Merit, but this is an old argument, the kind that tends to spawn pages upon pages of debate and I don't want to derail this thread. So I'll just say that I disagree and if you're interested in discussing it further we should do it in another thread or private messages.</div> </div> </div> </div> Please would you explain it here?<br /> <br /> Arguments so far:<br /> <br /> 1. The Ordo doesn't use human ways and methods.<br /> Fact: The Ordo book has quite a large section talking about how they use modern science.<br /> <br /> 2. The Ordo isn't about benefiting others.<br /> Fact: Many of the scales can be used to benefit others.<br /> <br /> Any more arguments?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":299,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","user":"NineDaysDead","date":". 05-24-2015, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T03:17:40-07:00","id":526507,"title":"","content":"Carthians take up human ways and methods. Like surgery.<br /> <br /> Ordo dracul are more on a long history kind of thing and on more a magical level of thought. <br /> <br /> I think this is the gist of the argument for Night Doctor Surgery to be Carthian.<br /> <br /> And I sorta agree. BUt I also think that a specific more Ordo-Like merit would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T03:33:33-07:00","id":526513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=526507#post526507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carthians take up human ways and methods. Like surgery.<br /> <br /> Ordo dracul are more on a long history kind of thing and on more a magical level of thought.<br /> <br /> I think this is the gist of the argument for Night Doctor Surgery to be Carthian.<br /> <br /> And I sorta agree. BUt I also think that a specific more Ordo-Like merit would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://snag.gy/oaiRR.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That sure looks like the Ordo is doing surgery to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The big picture: The dead scientist who experiments on humans, werewolves, and fairies in a sterile white laboratory. </div> </div> </div> Suggests they use &quot;human ways and methods. Like surgery&quot; and don't <i>only</i> use &quot;a magical level of thought&quot;, though they certainly do more mystical means too.<br /> <br /> The Ordo book has a whole section saying a lot of younger Dragons use modern science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":299,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","user":"NineDaysDead","date":". 05-24-2015, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T03:37:54-07:00","id":526518,"title":"","content":"The purpose of a surgery is to reverse, reduce, or end the damage caused by disease or injury to the tissue or organs of the patient. Carthians use Night Doctory Surgery to that end, for the benefit of the patient. The Ordo Dracul doesn't conduct surgery. They perform operations to benefit the practitioner, not their test subject.<br /> Yes, individual Dragons may put the Night Doctor Surgery merit to legitimate use, but concern for the well-being of others runs contrary to the default presentation of Ordo Dracul members and the system mechanics presented for developing and learning Scales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T04:02:57-07:00","id":526524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=526518#post526518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purpose of a surgery is to reverse, reduce, or end the damage caused by disease or injury to the tissue or organs of the patient. Carthians use Night Doctory Surgery to that end, for the benefit of the patient. The Ordo Dracul doesn't conduct surgery. They perform operations to benefit the practitioner, not their test subject.<br /> Yes, individual Dragons may put the Night Doctor Surgery merit to legitimate use, but concern for the well-being of others runs contrary to the default presentation of Ordo Dracul members and the system mechanics presented for developing and learning Scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's incorrect. Many scales can be used to benefit others:<br /> <br /> Day-Wake Conditioning<br /> Epidermal Shielding Bath<br /> Flesh Graft Treatment<br /> <br /> Surgical Heart Removal<br /> <br /> Blood Cleansing Ritual","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T04:15:34-07:00","id":526528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=526518#post526518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, individual Dragons may put the Night Doctor Surgery merit to legitimate use, but concern for the well-being of others runs contrary to the default presentation of Ordo Dracul members and the system mechanics presented for developing and learning Scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Ordo members sadly cannot put the merit to use, at least under the current rules (and hence my point). A prerequisite for the Night Doctor Surgery merit is membership in the Carthians. I would suggest a more appropriate prerequisite would simply be a few dots in Medicine and Occult, rather than limiting availability of the merit based on Covenant.<br /> <br /> I believe the original intent of Night Doctor Surgery was to invoke the imagery of back-room clinics and organized crime from modern media which often thematically characterizes the Carthians. I certainly do not object to Cathians having the merit, but its nature seems to fit squarely within the experience, skill and specializations concerning vampire physiology which typify the Ordo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T04:22:44-07:00","id":526530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=526528#post526528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I believe the original intent of Night Doctor Surgery was to invoke the imagery of back-room clinics and organized crime from modern media which often thematically characterizes the Carthians.</div> </div> </div> </div> That imagery would also support the Invictus having it, as &quot;the Conspiracy of Silence&quot; has quite a few old school mafia similarities. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T04:31:38-07:00","id":526533,"title":"","content":"I don't really see the problem here. It would be trivial to just port over the mechanics to a scale. Plus it means you'd potentially get Dragons accusing the Carthians of stealing secrets, for which the Carthians would accuse the Dragons of malicious slander and so on. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T08:04:23-07:00","id":526666,"title":"","content":"Ok, so here's my take on the matter. Night doctor surgery adapts human surgical techniques to be used on Kindred. I don't think anyone disagrees that's right up the Carthians' alley, adapting human practices to Kindred needs. That's not to say the Ordo couldn't or wouldn't use these techniques if they knew how to. However, the ability to heal other vampires through human surgery doesn't advance their goals of defying the curse, and therefore I don't see them dedicating energy to developing such techniques. Especially when they've already got Flesh Graft Treatment.<br /> <br /> Now, the argument seems not to be that Night Doctor Surgery should be an Ordo-only Merit, but that it would fit well with the Ordo as well as the Carthians. And I agree, even though I don't see the majority of the Ordo researching into such things, I could see certain individuals that would have interest in it. But tge Carthians developed it, and go to great lengths to keep it a secret, even going so far as to hide the identities of their surgeons. That doesn't mean a clever Dragon couldn't develop the same or similar techniques independently, but such a thing would, I think, be the focus of a story or chronicle. And, of course, the fact that Nighr Doctor Surgery requires two dots of Carthian Status to learn doesn't actually prevent Ordo Dracul members from buying the Merit, since in 2e you can have status in multiple Covenants. You'd require three dots of Ordo Status as well, but it makes sense to me that in order to learn the secret surgical techniques of the Carthians, a Dragon would need to be in high standing within his own Covenant, and have excellent relations with the Carthians.<br /> <br /> So that's my stance on the matter. Though, as Elfive pointed out, if you disagree with all of that, it is pretty easy to just change the prerequisite in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T10:56:37-07:00","id":526839,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the Carthian covenant book seems to suggest that &quot;Thanatology&quot; (the study of Kindred physiology) is a bit more involved than just applying human sciences to the Kindred body, so it might not be that Dragons don't know how to do the mortal science, so much as they don't know the Thanatology, and the Carthians won't just teach it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T13:48:13-07:00","id":527007,"title":"","content":"See, that's an even weaker argument against the Defiant figuring it out. If anyone is going to have a handle on kindred physiology, it's going to be the guys studying, codifying, and improving it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:07:38-07:00","id":527040,"title":"","content":"There definitely doesn't seem to be one method to rule them all to understand Kindred physiology. I don't really see the issue with the idea that the Ordo and the Carthians have come up with radically different methods to interact with Kindred physiology, that produce different results. Just because you know one way to do it doesn't mean you'll definitely know another, especially if nobody taught it to you.<br /> <br /> I don't really care if Carthians have exclusive access to the merit, do as you'd like in your game. I just think it makes sense that the two covenants approach similar-ISH things (Night Doctors aren't really similar to Ordo Dracul Scales) in different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-24-2015, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:19:06-07:00","id":527081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=526530#post526530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That imagery would also support the Invictus having it, as &quot;the Conspiracy of Silence&quot; has quite a few old school mafia similarities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, and quite frankly could also envision similar thematic reasons why the LeS and the Crone, particularly with their more magical leanings, might develop skills and procedures to accomplish results identical to the Night Doctor Surgery merit. It's the reason why I suggested that the merit should only have skill prerequisites in Medicine and Occult, rather than any Covenant limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T22:47:15-07:00","id":527363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=526528#post526528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Ordo members sadly cannot put the merit to use, at least under the current rules (and hence my point). A prerequisite for the Night Doctor Surgery merit is membership in the Carthians. I would suggest a more appropriate prerequisite would simply be a few dots in Medicine and Occult, rather than limiting availability of the merit based on Covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually they can, It takes 2 dots in carthian status, if memory serves, maybe three? <br /> <br /> Vampires can have five dots in covenant status, which means one could be a night doctor and a dragon of good standing.<br /> <br /> There's also a carthian merit that opens up carthian status to not count to that five dot limit, so with that a night doctor could even have 5 dots of status in ordo dracul.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now I agree with the premise that it makes sense to me for dragons to have this knowledge too, since it's kind of their thing, but dragons aren't barred from it under the rules, a carthian dragon is quite possible. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T23:30:08-07:00","id":527376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=527363#post527363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually they can, It takes 2 dots in carthian status, if memory serves, maybe three?<br /> <br /> Vampires can have five dots in covenant status, which means one could be a night doctor and a dragon of good standing.<br /> <br /> There's also a carthian merit that opens up carthian status to not count to that five dot limit, so with that a night doctor could even have 5 dots of status in ordo dracul.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now I agree with the premise that it makes sense to me for dragons to have this knowledge too, since it's kind of their thing, but dragons aren't barred from it under the rules, a carthian dragon is quite possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I stand corrected.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> However, the permutations you describe wherein a Dragon has managed two or more dots of Cathian Status (and limiting his Ordo Satatus) and able to choose the Night Doctor Surgery merit would be <i>very </i>highly unusual, and undoubtedly far more the exception than rule.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it also doesn't account for <i>why</i> Carthians (or a vampire with more than nominal Cathian Status), among all the Covenants, somehow have a near monopoly on the techniques to perform undead surgery. Again, I'm just curious as to the justification / game design decision for limiting the merit by Covenant, rather than skill set (and, of course, I know I can do whatever I want in my own games). The fact that Dragons' interests, abilities and experience so closely parallel the particular merit simply heightens my curiosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-25-2015, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:02:54-07:00","id":527577,"title":"","content":"I think it mostly boils down to the fact that it was conceptualized and written for the Carthian covenant book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:45:55-07:00","id":527614,"title":"","content":"Covenents do not create new technologies and powers. Individuals create technology and powers. Covenents only disseminate or restrict access to that new thing after it's been made. One day, some dude invented Night Doctor Surgery. That dude just so happened to be a Carthian. He taught his Carthian brothers and the Carthians put a patent on it and stopped people from teaching it outside the Carthians.<br /> <br /> Why was this guy a Carthian? Probably random luck, mostly. But if I were to attach some greater meaning behind it, it's that necessity is the mother of invention. Carthians (at least those on the front line) often to ballsy, stupid, risky things. They get hurt. They developed techniques to help with that.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracule simply get hurt less and are thus less incentivized to develop that technology, especially after Flesh Graft Treatment became widely available. I mean you can spend tons of resources and effort to create a technique that has a widely available and arguably &quot;better&quot; equivalent already, or you can spend your time researching something more productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:20:12-07:00","id":527759,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt;<i> More importantly, it also doesn't account for why Carthians (or a vampire with more than nominal Cathian Status), among all the Covenants, somehow have a near monopoly on the techniques to perform undead surgery. </i><i>&gt;&gt;</i><br /> <br /> Because the Carthian Movement infiltrated the medical profession and established the necessary connections and social networks required to develop the Night Doctors' surgical procedures used tonight over a century before the individuals who would become the first Ordo Dracul members were old enough to read a copy of Mary Shelley's <i>Frankenstein</i>.<br /> <br /> If you're a vampire desperate or vain enough to willingly put yourself under the knife of someone you can't control via vinculum or disciplines, who are you going to submit to: Dr. Teeth, the obviously disguised Carthian with known connections in the medical field all over the city (that you can ferret out if he screws you). Or Dr. Madblood, who works out of the split level ranch he bought ten years ago because it belonged to a serial killer (and site of a wyrm's nest) and converted it into a funeral home which is also used for Ordo Dracul tea time (a euphemism for their publicized chapterhouse experiments).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:47:31-07:00","id":528013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=527614#post527614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why was this guy a Carthian? Probably random luck, mostly. But if I were to attach some greater meaning behind it, it's that necessity is the mother of invention. Carthians (at least those on the front line) often to ballsy, stupid, risky things. They get hurt. They developed techniques to help with that.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracule simply get hurt less and are thus less incentivized to develop that technology, especially after Flesh Graft Treatment became widely available. I mean you can spend tons of resources and effort to create a technique that has a widely available and arguably &quot;better&quot; equivalent already, or you can spend your time researching something more productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a very good reason, the Ordo probably came up with a handful of Scales (not just Flesh Graft Treatment, although that might be the only one left) to deal with getting hurt before surgery seriously moved past 'cut it out/off' (which requires both anaesthetic and antibiotics/abiotic treatment to properly do for humans), and they may well have a 'surgery scale' that uses human surgery techniques but enhanced to make them more efficient (300 year old vampires use a variation of 'cut it out quickly', whereas modern Dragons may well use more complex surgery). When they learnt more complex surgery techniques they adapted the Scale to work with them, instead of the other way around.<br /> <br /> The Carthians, on the other hand, probably relied on 'use Vitae to heal' a lot more than they would have liked, until some doctors that joined had the idea of adapting surgery techniques to work on Kindred. Unlike the Ordo, they couldn't use existing scales to cheat, and so spent a long time developing and improving the Night Doctor Surgery techniques. The Ordo suspects that they just stole their Scale, but they have no proof, and they seem to do it with comparatively minimalistic supplies.<br /> <br /> The Invictus are just too used to going to other Covenants for this stuff to have spent time developing it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:13:14-07:00","id":528309,"title":"","content":"The simplest answer?<br /> <br /> A Carthian figured it out. A Dragon didn't. The Carthians only recently figured it out, and have done a pretty good job of keeping tight-lipped.<br /> <br /> Just because a group seems like the logical group to come up with something, doesn't mean they did. This is the case in real world history and innovation as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:43:45-07:00","id":528369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=528309#post528309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest answer?<br /> <br /> A Carthian figured it out. A Dragon didn't. The Carthians only recently figured it out, and have done a pretty good job of keeping tight-lipped.<br /> <br /> Just because a group seems like the logical group to come up with something, doesn't mean they did. This is the case in real world history and innovation as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you believe is the real world history and innovation / thematic analog for Carthians exclusively having the Night Doctor Surgery merit. I earlier posited that it's reminiscent of back room medical clinics and organized crime.<br /> <br /> It also good to see it has no quasi-mystical justification similar to Carthian Law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-25-2015, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:46:53-07:00","id":528457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/526479-night-doctor-surgery-discussion?p=528369#post528369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What do you believe is the real world history and innovation / thematic analog for Carthians exclusively having the Night Doctor Surgery merit. I earlier posited that it's reminiscent of back room medical clinics and organized crime.<br /> <br /> It also good to see it has no quasi-mystical justification similar to Carthian Law.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look at it like mob doctors, similarly.<br /> <br /> I also don't think it's spread enough beyond rumour for the Dragons to care much. I think if word got out, some might be interested in finding out more. But the party line is that they're not doctors, they're not studying in order to repair damage. It'd be useful to better understand how this works, but for the same reason a surgeon would be well-served to know Latin. The Latin doesn't actually help him with his surgery, but the mutual language does have its benefits in discussion of the craft.<br /> <br /> I'll also note, this is purely my opinion. I only wrote the Second Edition version of the Merit. I liked it. I played a Carthian with that Merit for a long time, and felt it delivered a lot to play. But, I left it open because I felt that was the best avenue to take. Sometimes, I prefer to leave questions to ask and answer at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T05:46:42-07:00","id":530914,"title":"","content":"Short Answer<br /> Nigh Doctors were a faction of the 1st edition Carthians. The Shift in the themes of second edition Ordo seems fit better with Night surgery for some people.<br /> me meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}